    {
      "id": 54,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -253.48050792431238,
        -1143.2412206462595
      ],
      "size": [
        561.0930134309751,
        445.04052940435054
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 12,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Markdkberry.com\n\nZ image model for i2i workflow. specifically low denoise fixing of plastic skin issues.\n\n## models\n\n- int8 model can download from here [https://huggingface.co/Winnougan/Z-Image-Base-Turbo-INT8-Convrot/tree/main](https://huggingface.co/Winnougan/Z-Image-Base-Turbo-INT8-Convrot/tree/main) including the text encoder version. This is ideal for lowVRAM GPUs and to be honest I could not see any difference compared to the below full size models. </br>\n\n- I originally used fp8 and turbo bf16 models along with a full size text encoder. from here [https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Z-Image-Turbo/tree/main/split_files/diffusion_models](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Z-Image-Turbo/tree/main/split_files/diffusion_models)\n\n## Issues\n\n- **dappling occurs with turbo models**. I use very low denoise for fixing skin and low enough it works okay for that but can also impact clothing. It looks like paper effect on everything, dappling blotches and is a know issue. I have not solved it, only mitigated it. That was with bf16 and fp8 turbo models. I plan to test int 8 convrot models next. (turbo).\n    - **for fixing skin reduce the denoise down to 0.03 really that low is good enough for subtle skin improvement of plastic faces**. going to 0.1 it will dapple especially noticeably on clothing. I havent solved it, but for skin realism this works okay. </br>\n   - **reducing aura flow to between 3 and 6** actually helped for me.\n\n\n\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "# Markdkberry.com\n\nZ image model for i2i workflow. specifically low denoise fixing of plastic skin issues.\n\n## models\n\n- int8 model can download from here [https://huggingface.co/Winnougan/Z-Image-Base-Turbo-INT8-Convrot/tree/main](https://huggingface.co/Winnougan/Z-Image-Base-Turbo-INT8-Convrot/tree/main) including the text encoder version. This is ideal for lowVRAM GPUs and to be honest I could not see any difference compared to the below full size models. </br>\n\n- I originally used fp8 and turbo bf16 models along with a full size text encoder. from here [https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Z-Image-Turbo/tree/main/split_files/diffusion_models](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Z-Image-Turbo/tree/main/split_files/diffusion_models)\n\n## Issues\n\n- **dappling occurs with turbo models**. I use very low denoise for fixing skin and low enough it works okay for that but can also impact clothing. It looks like paper effect on everything, dappling blotches and is a know issue. I have not solved it, only mitigated it. That was with bf16 and fp8 turbo models. I plan to test int 8 convrot models next. (turbo).\n    - **for fixing skin reduce the denoise down to 0.03 really that low is good enough for subtle skin improvement of plastic faces**. going to 0.1 it will dapple especially noticeably on clothing. I havent solved it, but for skin realism this works okay. </br>\n   - **reducing aura flow to between 3 and 6** actually helped for me.\n\n\n\n"
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
